-- title:
--   Ribet level raising in support form for odd p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $q'$ be a prime not dividing $N$ (with $Nq' \neq 0$), and let $f$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form for $\Gamma_0(N)$ which is a normalised eigenform in the sense of [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L28): its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1(f) = 1$, $a_{mn}(f) = a_m(f)a_n(f)$ for coprime $m,n$, $a_{\ell^{r+2}}(f) = a_\ell(f)a_{\ell^{r+1}}(f) - \ell\, a_{\ell^{r}}(f)$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, and $a_{\ell^{r+2}}(f) = a_\ell(f) a_{\ell^{r+1}}(f)$ for primes $\ell \mid N$. Let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a maximal ideal of $\overline{\mathbf{Z}} = \operatorname{integralClosure} \mathbf{Z}\, \mathbf{C}$ containing $p$, and let $\chi_1$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra (N * q') 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N * q'}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbf{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbf{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(Nq'))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid Nq'$ — to $\overline{\mathbf{Z}}$ with $\chi_1(T_\ell) = a_\ell(f)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid Nq'$. Assume given $a_{q'} \in \overline{\mathbf{Z}}$ whose image in $\mathbf{C}$ is $a_{q'}(f)$, that $a_{q'}^2 - (q'+1)^2 \in \mathfrak{m}$, and that $\mathfrak{m}$ is non-Eisenstein along $\chi_1$ at some prime $\ell \nmid Nq'$ with $\ell \neq p$, i.e. $\chi_1(T_\ell) - (\ell + 1) \notin \mathfrak{m}$. Let $A$ be an Atkin–Lehner datum for $q'$ at level $Nq'$, that is, a factorisation $Nq' = q' R$ together with integers $a,b$ satisfying $q'a - Rb = 1$. Then every $T$ in the Hecke algebra which annihilates, as an endomorphism of $S_2(\Gamma_0(Nq'))$, the intersection of the kernels of the trace map $g \mapsto g + U_{q'}(g\mid_2 W_A)$ and of its composite with $g \mapsto g \mid_2 W_A$ lies in $\chi_1^{-1}(\mathfrak{m})$.
--
--   This is Ribet's level-raising theorem in support (annihilator) form: under the congruence $a_{q'}(f)^2 \equiv (q'+1)^2$ modulo $\mathfrak m$ and non-Eisenstein-ness at one auxiliary prime $\ell \neq p$, the maximal ideal $\chi_1^{-1}(\mathfrak m)$ attached to the $q'$-old copy of $f$ lies in the support of the $q'$-new subspace at level $Nq'$, the hypothesis on $p$ being only that it is odd. It is used to produce a newform at level $Nq'$ congruent to $f$ modulo $\mathfrak m$, as consumed by [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_isNewAt_congr_of_levelRaisingCongruence`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_isNewAt_congr_of_levelRaisingCongruence).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LevelRaising_qNewSupport_comap_of_isNormalizedEigenform_oddPrime.lean

import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_LevelLoweringTrace
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_AtkinLehnerOperator

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
